00:22:39,817 --> 00:22:45,463
And while he was there at the Mahasi Centre, he went through all these vipassana and jhanas.

203
00:22:46,464 --> 00:22:50,730
He told me, and the way he explained them, he'd obviously done it, and they told him he'd done it.

204
00:22:51,549 --> 00:22:52,672
And then he went back home.

205
00:22:52,711 --> 00:23:02,281
When he came back to the monastery the next year to practice, and by the way, he knew virtually, you know, he only knew the surface understandings of Buddhism.

206
00:23:02,768 --> 00:23:10,400
When he went back to practice, the monks at the Mahasi center were sort of a bit mystified as to why he hadn't become a Buddhist.

207
00:23:10,901 --> 00:23:13,345
He was still a very committed Christian.

208
00:23:13,365 --> 00:23:25,063
So it just shows you that Buddhism, Christianity, Islam, they're the next level of understanding coming from certain cultural traditions, et cetera, but anybody

209
00:23:25,381 --> 00:23:46,730
can come to the vipassana and just observe just feel just see and keep looking at this reactive reaction within us to see impermanence and to create that distance and know that everything's happening not directly under our control these are the insights that lead to liberation

210
00:23:47,487 --> 00:23:59,203
So having said that, I hope those of you who would have feared that you'd have to go into an MA or a PhD in this stuff before you became liberated are relieved.

211
00:24:00,005 --> 00:24:07,936
And I can only hope that by your practice you will in fact be relieved of all your suffering sooner rather than later.

212
00:24:09,779 --> 00:24:10,760
So we can do a bit of practice.

213
00:24:28,257 --> 00:24:29,627
Oh, yeah.

